Shared (dynamic) library - LGPL, dynamically linked for compliance
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

GMP (GNU Multiple Precision Arithmetic Library)
  License: LGPL v3 (some files GPL v2+)
  Linking: dynamic
    macOS:  Homebrew ("brew install gmp"); the build bundles
            libgmp.10.dylib next to lumyr using @loader_path, so users
            may replace it with their own build (LGPL relinking right).
    Linux:  distribution package (libgmp-dev), libgmp.so.10
    Windows: prebuilt/windows/bin/libgmp-10.dll (built from source by
             scripts/build_deps_mingw.sh, with lib/libgmp.dll.a import
             library), copied next to lumyr.exe at build time
  License texts: deps/gmp/licenses/
  Source:   https://gmplib.org/

---------------------------------------------------------------------------
System libraries (provided by the OS, not redistributed by this product)
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

On macOS and Linux the following facilities are provided by the operating
system's own libraries and are not bundled with this product:

  HTTP client : libcurl (macOS: /usr/lib/libcurl.4.dylib;
                Linux: distribution package)
  Charset conv: iconv (POSIX; macOS /usr/lib/libiconv.2.dylib)
  Regex       : POSIX regex.h (libc)

Their use is governed by the platform's own terms (macOS: Apple software
license; Linux: respective distribution licenses).

Build-time requirements:
  macOS:  brew install gmp bison flex
  Linux:  libgmp-dev, bison, flex (distribution packages)

