Windows (MinGW-w64) - prebuilt third-party components
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

libcurl 8.22.0
  License: MIT/X derivate (https://curl.se/docs/copyright.html)
  Linking: static; TLS backend is Windows Schannel (-lsecur32)
  License text: prebuilt/windows/licenses/libcurl/

libiconv 1.17
  License: LGPL v2.1
  Linking: dynamic (libiconv-2.dll, shipped next to lumyr.exe)
  License text: prebuilt/windows/licenses/libiconv/

TRE 0.9.0
  License: BSD 2-Clause
  Linking: static; used solely as the POSIX regex.h implementation that
  Windows lacks (no approximate-matching features are used)
  License text: prebuilt/windows/licenses/tre/

GMP 6.3.0
  License: LGPL v3 (some files GPL v2+) - see the GMP section above
  Linking: dynamic (bin/libgmp-10.dll shipped next to lumyr.exe,
  linked via lib/libgmp.dll.a)
  License text: deps/gmp/licenses/

Build tools on Windows: WinFlexBison (flex 2.6.4 / bison 3.8.2),
build-time only; generated parsers are covered by the flex/bison runtime
exceptions. The Windows libraries (curl/iconv/tre/gmp) are all rebuilt
from source via scripts/build_deps_mingw.sh in an MSYS2 MINGW64
environment (MINGW32 for 32-bit).

The third-party components above are not part of the compiler's own
source code.
